sentences.text:
5. Accordingly, the Criminal Appeal is allowed and the appellant is directed to be enlarged on bail on condition that the appellant shall execute a bond for a sum of Rs.10,000/-(Rupees Ten Thousand Only), with two sureties, each for a like sum to the satisfaction of the learned Principal District and Sessions Judge, Thiruvallur and on further condition that:
(a) the sureties shall affix their photographs and left thumb impression in the surety bond and the Court concerned may obtain a copy of their Aadhar card or Bank pass Book to ensure their identity;
(b) the appellant shall report before the respondent police daily at 10.30 a.m. until Page No:3/6 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis further orders;

(c) the appellant shall not tamper with evidence or witness either during investigation or trial;
